        "original_id": "5fd4a946-5192-5abc-a780-5a3d519c05ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fort Hunter, Albany County, Schenectady, Rotterdam, Downtown Schenectady\n- Roads: New York Route 146, Interstate 890, Interstate 90, New York State Route 7, Watt Street\n- Products: Crosstown Plaza\n\nFacts:\n- Fort Hunter lies along New York Route 146 near the Albany–Schenectady county line.\n- Interstate 890 is a 9.45-mile auxiliary Interstate Highway in the vicinity of Schenectady, New York.\n- Interstate 890 runs southeast–northwest from an interchange with the New York State Thruway (Interstate 90) northwest of Schenectady to another junction with the Thruway south of the city.\n- Interstate 890 passes through Downtown Schenectady.\n- Crosstown Plaza is a large strip mall in Schenectady at the Rotterdam–Schenectady line.\n- Crosstown Plaza is located along Watt Street and New York State Route 7 near an entrance to Interstate 890.",
